@startuml seq-hand-admin
title Hand admin plane — one shared token for every hand (F3)

participant "serve" as serve
participant "atenet (Envoy)\nHost-header routing" as net
participant "hand h-<sid>" as hand
participant "another session's hand\nh-<other>" as other

serve -> net : POST /admin/identity  {session, actor}
net -> hand : Host: h-<sid>.agents…
serve -> net : POST /admin/upstreams {mcp servers + headers}
net -> hand : (federates user's MCP servers, with credentials)
serve -> net : POST /admin/grant {grant, names}
net -> hand : (hand then pulls values — see seq-vault-grant)
hand -> hand : adminAuthed(): compare Bearer to HAND_ADMIN_TOKEN

note over hand, other #FFE4E4
  The token is <b>the same in every hand</b> (one Secret, mounted everywhere)
  and it is <b>also the grant-signing key</b> (serve.go:174).
  With <b>no NetworkPolicy (F5)</b>, model-generated code in one hand can:
   1. read its own env → obtain the token,
   2. reach h-<other> directly → drive another session's admin plane,
   3. sign its own grants → pull ANY user's vault credentials.
  Fix: separate keys + per-session tokens + ActorIdentity binding.
end note
hand -[#CC0000]-> other : lateral movement (possible today)
@enduml
